OL,3,ABadenoch defends amputee marathon
OL,4,Arunners claim in benefits cut row
OL,5,
OL,6,FConservative leader Kemi Badenoch has
OL,7,Fdefended her suggestion that because
OL,8,Fdouble amputees run marathons more
OL,9,Fdisabled people should work instead of
OL,10,Fclaiming benefits.
OL,12,FBadenoch had used the example when
OL,13,Fsetting out her party's plans to cut
OL,14,Fwelfare spending by #36bn a year.
OL,16,FHer comments were criticised by
OL,17,FParalympian Richard Whitehead, who
OL,18,Faccused her of "weaponising" his
OL,19,Fsporting success, while Prime Minister
OL,20,FAndy Burnham called the Tory leader's
OL,21,Fwords "crass and insensitive".
OL,23,APub: 19-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,311,300,200,140,0,100
