OL,3,ABadenoch defends amputee marathon
OL,4,Arunners claim in benefits cut row
OL,5,
OL,6,FBut in an interview with the BBC Radio
OL,7,F4's Today programme, Badenoch stood by
OL,8,Fthe remarks, insisting that "if people
OL,9,Feven with significant problems can
OL,10,Fwork, then those who have ADHD and mild
OL,11,Fanxiety should go to work".
